    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d236">

                <pb facs="0511" n="427" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg427"/>

                <head>No. 232.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir L.
                            West to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-11-12"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 12, 1886</date>.
                        [Received November 12.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of yesterday’s date, together with certain statements in which
                    complaint is made of the conduct of the collector of customs at Shelburne, Nova
                    Scotia, and the conduct of Captain Quigley, of the Canadian cruiser Terror, in
                    their dealings with certain American fishing vessels, and to inform you that I
                    have forwarded the same to Her Majesty’s Government.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>L. S. SACKVILLE WEST.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
